From 5b265ce676f8d1bd57529d48be7da76e157a0523 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sanford Lincoln <github@heysanford.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 06:32:56 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kitty): give the placement's size in cells (c/r)

iTerm2 draws Kitty unicode-placeholder images only when the virtual
placement says how many cells it spans. Without c/r it draws nothing,
and since iTerm2 answers the Kitty query, the picker chooses Kitty there
by default. Kitty and Ghostty infer the size from the pixel size, which
goes wrong whenever that doesn't match their cell size exactly.

Both transmit paths (base64 and shared memory) now send c/r from the
Size that Kitty::new and StatefulKitty::resize_encode already have.

Refs #158

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/protocol/kitty.rs | 111 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----------
 1 file changed, 85 insertions(+), 26 deletions(-)

